  (text "1) 12 V INPUT + BUCK 12 V -> 5 V" (at 40.64 13.97 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54)) (justify left top))
    (uuid acf0740d-b04d-520e-9aff-136baf2e0dae)
  )
  (text "+12V and GND come from the Gree board LOGIC side through J1 (+12V pad and 'GND', never 'GND/').\nF1 limits fault current into the Gree 12 V rail; D1 blocks back-feed when the board is powered from J5." (at 40.64 18.415 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 4e08ff2a-68fe-5b71-9cbd-998866e0be47)
  )
  (text "2) 5 V -> 3.3 V LDO" (at 175.26 13.97 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 93b6358d-d33f-5f60-b52c-f248170bd25b)
  )
  (text "D2 lets J5 (USB-UART adapter 5 V) power the board on the bench.\nThe 5 V rail only feeds the LDO (all level shifting runs at 3.3 V)." (at 175.26 18.415 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid b2c9ed65-8c05-53e2-9dd7-ac5b96077e29)
  )
  (text "4) IR LINE + BUS TAPS (5 V -> 3.3 V)" (at 43.18 83.82 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 38af2a95-fed2-5480-815a-c64f1d9a8c9d)
  )
  (text "J1 (one 5-pin JST XH, 2.50 mm, shared ground) on the Gree indoor board LOGIC side:\n  1 +12V    2 IR data line (5 V)    3 RX tap: U6 opto output, pin 4 (0.10 V / 1.07 V); the 5 V MCU RX line also works\n  4 TX tap: Gree board's TX opto (its U3) drive node, logic side    5 GND ('GND', never 'GND/')\nIR line and TX tap: 1k series + 1M bleed + 100pF -> bridge U3 74LVC14 Schmitt inverter (VCC 3.3 V, 5 V tolerant inputs), ~1 Mohm load.\nRX tap: 47k -> BC847 base (on above ~0.55 V, 1M pull-down, 100pF filter), 22k collector pull-up -> 74LVC14.\nIt takes ~10 uA from the U6 node, so the Gree board's own RX transistor keeps working normally.\nTransmit: BSS138 open drain, pulls IR_LINE low only while IR_TX is high; R9 keeps it off during boot/reset.\nBridge U3 inverts: IR decoding is edge-timing based, and gree_bus.be detects the bus UART polarity (BusAuto)." (at 40.64 205.74 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 95cef1dd-0ec4-54ac-994a-b6cb1dde7044)
  )
  (text "3) ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8" (at 142.24 83.82 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54)) (justify left top))
    (uuid f5ab7eeb-9dad-5443-80e3-79a20c03a670)
  )
  (text "ESP32: used pins sit on the side facing their circuit; every other GPIO is left open (NC flags).\nStrapping pins IO0/IO3/IO45/IO46: only IO0 is used (BOOT button).\nIO35/IO36/IO37 MUST stay unconnected: the octal PSRAM of the N16R8 uses them internally." (at 185.42 205.74 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 4a4bd139-d612-5790-b26a-f48715cd9018)
  )
  (text "5) I2C: BME280 on the board + J3 for more sensors" (at 205.74 189.23 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 291b7496-2b6a-5e13-87e0-d4b4f3fc25fb)
  )
  (text "U5: GY-BME280 breakout soldered at the bottom-right board edge, on a slotted island without copper pour,\naway from the regulators and the ESP32. Address 0x76 (SDO low). J3: more I2C sensors on a cable (3V3 GND SCL SDA)." (at 205.74 193.675 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 8f11acc6-d472-59ff-949d-29afe33edb78)
  )
  (text "PROGRAMMING (3.3 V-logic USB-UART)" (at 264.16 96.52 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left top))
    (uuid baff85e0-561a-51c9-b073-e8682c0cb3d7)
  )
  (text "Labels connect by name to the same\nlabels at the ESP32 and D2." (at 264.16 100.965 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid a52293b5-f05c-50c4-8639-40ffabc5194c)
  )
  (text "Hold BOOT, tap RESET to flash.\nAdapter RX -> pin 3, TX -> pin 4.\nAfter the first flash use OTA." (at 264.16 130.81 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid d8f628c5-139d-5800-9b04-507eee81c773)
  )
